* PUT - REDIRECT CONSOLE OR PRINTER OUTPUT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* PUT - REDIRECT CONSOLE OR PRINTER OUTPUT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:PUT CONSOLE FILE filespec [options]
    SYSUTLS:PUT CONSOLE CONSOLE
    SYSUTLS:PUT PRINTER FILE filespec [options]
    SYSUTLS:PUT PRINTER PRINTER

Captures the selected output stream in a disk file. Normally applies to
the next program; [SYSTEM] keeps redirection active across system
commands. [ECHO] or [NO ECHO] controls whether the captured stream also
reaches its device.

Example: SYSUTLS:PUT CONSOLE FILE I0:OUTPUT.TXT

Restore console output with SYSUTLS:PUT CONSOLE CONSOLE and printer output
with SYSUTLS:PUT PRINTER PRINTER. Check free space and avoid capturing
credentials or private caller information.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
